# Sync feature checklist

When adding or changing a **business entity** (new Drift table, new fields, CRUD, list/detail UI), complete the sync-related items below. Pattern reference: transactions + `SyncTables` / `PendingSyncCornerBadge` / `PendingSyncDetailBadge`.

## Data model

- Add `isNotSynced` (default `true`) and soft-delete via `isDeleted` — **never hard-delete** synced business rows.
- On create/update/soft-delete, set `isNotSynced: true` (and `updatedAt`).
- Prefer **update in place** by stable UUID. Soft-delete a child line only when the user explicitly removes it — do not replace-all lines on every save.

## Sync engine wiring

Canonical list: `lib/features/backup/data/sync/sync_tables.dart` (`SyncTables`).

- Register new tables in `SyncTables.ordered` in **FK-safe** order.
- Map table → Drift `TableInfo` in `SyncTables.tableInfo` / `allKnownTableInfos`.
- Add datetime columns to `SyncTables.dateFields` if needed.
- Remap legacy/alias names via `sqlTableName` when SQL name ≠ payload name.
- Ensure push (`_getLocalChanges`), apply, mark-synced, unsynced counts, and reset-local-sync all use `SyncTables` (do not maintain a separate table list).

## Dashboard “changes to push”

- Group the new table under a feature group in `_groupUnsyncedBreakdown` (`sync_status_section.dart`).
- Add localized table label in `_syncTableLabel` (EN / HI / UR).
- Drill-down must still show **per-table** counts (group total + expand).
- Navigation should open the correct screen (AppBar/back or parent tab with `initialTab` when embedded).

## UI pending-sync indicators

- **List items**: `PendingSyncCornerBadge` when `isNotSynced == true` (same as transaction list).
- **Detail heroes/headers**: `PendingSyncDetailBadge` as a **corner overlay** on a full-width card (`width: double.infinity` if content would otherwise shrink-wrap). Do not use a text chip in the header.
- Use `l10n.pendingSync` for tooltips.

## Watchers / refresh

- Include the table in backup unsynced-count watch streams when relevant.
- After sync apply, Drift `markTablesUpdated` must cover the new table via `SyncTables.allKnownTableInfos`.

## Quick anti-patterns

- ❌ Soft-delete all children then insert new UUIDs on every edit
- ❌ Hard-delete rows “because they were never synced”
- ❌ New table in DB but missing from `SyncTables.ordered`
- ❌ Detail pending-sync chip instead of corner badge; shrink-wrapped hero with badge at screen edge
